WEBVTT

00:01:29.769 --> 00:01:32.743
We create spaces outside of convention,

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:34.879
including the conventions of time.

00:01:34.903 --> 00:01:37.956
And in those 3,000 messages between us,

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:39.218
we collapsed time;

00:01:39.242 --> 00:01:40.401
we queered it;

00:01:40.425 --> 00:01:42.187
we laid it all on the table.

00:01:42.211 --> 00:01:43.247
(Laughter)

00:01:43.271 --> 00:01:45.033
With no pretense at all.

00:01:45.513 --> 00:01:48.312
And this meant that we were able
to commit to each other

00:01:48.336 --> 00:01:49.933
in a profoundly different way.

00:01:50.496 --> 00:01:54.564
So often what we're told is this idea
of the "Golden Rule,"

00:01:54.588 --> 00:01:58.029
that we should treat other people
the way we want to be treated.

00:01:58.053 --> 00:01:59.409
But the problem with that

00:01:59.433 --> 00:02:02.664
is that it assumes that we are
the standard for other people,